H5P runtime assets — origin and licensing
==========================================

This directory bundles the H5P editor/player runtime so the service works fully
offline (hermetic deploy). None of it is authored here; each part keeps its
upstream license. See ../../THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the license summary.

core/     The H5P core runtime.
          Upstream: https://github.com/h5p/h5p-php-library  (tag 1.28.0,
                    commit 2aeb0b83fa603e331381b3a6b8bf42c3773ba140)
          License:  GPL-3.0 (The H5P Group / Joubel AS and contributors).
                    Verbatim upstream text in core/LICENSE.txt; confirmed by the
                    upstream composer.json ("license": "GPL-3.0").
          Fonts:    core/fonts/inter (Inter) and core/fonts/open-sans (Open
                    Sans v40) are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1; their
                    texts ship beside them (inter/LICENSE.txt, open-sans/OFL.txt).
                    The h5p-core-30, h5p-hub-publish and h5p-theme icon fonts
                    come with the core under its license.

editor/   The H5P editor client (the 1.27 line — core 1.28 needs no editor
          update, so core and editor are now different versions), including
          the bundled CKEditor 5 in editor/ckeditor.
          Upstream: https://github.com/h5p/h5p-editor-php-library
          License:  Declared inconsistently upstream — the README (which
                    package.json designates as the license) says MIT, while
                    composer.json says GPL-3.0. Details in editor/LICENSE.txt.
                    Original notices are preserved; the deployment layout
                    does not resolve this upstream discrepancy.

H5P content-type and editor-widget libraries are NOT bundled here. They are
untracked runtime data provisioned into .host-data/libraries at deploy time; see
scripts/provision-libraries.mjs and the generated THIRD-PARTY-LIBRARIES.md.

Provenance
----------
core/ is the runtime part (js/, styles/, fonts/, images/, LICENSE.txt) of the
upstream tag 1.28.0, fetched with scripts/fetch-h5p-assets.sh --core-only.
Before local patches it was byte-identical to the core inside h5p-standalone
3.8.2. Two local patches, marked in their source files on 2026-10-08 and kept
as patches/core/*.patch, fix:
  - js/h5p-tooltip.js: cancel pending hiding and retain hover state when the
    pointer enters the tooltip, so it remains readable under the pointer.
  - js/h5p-confirmation-dialog.js: restore the icon and spacing class on the
    legacy (non-themed) confirm button.
Before 1.28 the core was upstream master b5f527e, a post-1.27.0 snapshot that
an earlier version of this NOTICE called "1.27.0".

editor/ was copied from a vetted local checkout of the 1.27 line and carries
one local patch (scripts/h5peditor-metadata.js, kept as
patches/editor/0001-metadata-no-nameless-author.patch; it applies to upstream
h5p-editor-php-library 3bec2594, the file's only difference from it).

patches/  The local fixes above as unified diffs against upstream, one file
          per fix, applied in file-name order. They are not served.
          test/asset-patches.test.js checks that each one is present in the
          committed tree.

Licensing correction: an earlier version of this NOTICE stated that both
upstream repositories are "MIT-licensed, which permits this redistribution."
That is not accurate. The upstream core is GPL-3.0 (see core/LICENSE.txt), and
the editor's license is declared inconsistently upstream (see
editor/LICENSE.txt). These notices and the applicable distribution obligations
remain relevant regardless of where the runtime is deployed.

The CKEditor build has been identified independently: all 73 files match
h5p/h5p-editor-php-library commit 2db790c4df5398883492f49be5820522e22e1866.
This identifies CKEditor specifically; it does not assert that every other
editor asset came from that commit. The exact custom build and table-plugin
sources, checksums and verified rebuild instructions are in
../../docs/CKEDITOR_SOURCE.md and ../../sources/ckeditor5-source.json.

Upgrades
--------
`scripts/fetch-h5p-assets.sh [--core-only] [--no-patches] [core-ref]
[editor-ref]` re-fetches the runtime trees with their upstream LICENSE files,
applies patches/<tree>/*.patch and stages the result next to the current tree;
review the parity check before bumping the H5P version. The core and the
editor take separate refs: the core repository tags releases as `1.28.0` (not
`1.28`), the editor repository has no matching tags, so its ref (a branch or
commit) must be given explicitly. A patch that no longer applies stops the
script: rebase it onto the new upstream, or delete it when upstream has fixed
the issue, and update the list above. After replacing a tree run npm test and
npm run test:browser.

The core pin (1.28) MUST stay in sync with `src/h5p/config.ts`
(`coreApiVersion` / `h5pVersion`). Core files that h5p-server does not register
are added by `src/h5p/core-assets-hotfix.ts`; check that list on every core or
h5p-server update (test/core-assets-hotfix.test.js enforces it).
